<h2>2️⃣ CORE BUSINESS RULES - FINAL LOGIC</h2><div class="badge">
<b>Auto Allocate Learner ID:</b> Variable <code>learnerCounter</code> from localStorage mk_learnerCounter default 1 - Function <code>autoGenerateLearnerId()</code> generates L-0001 - In <code>addLearner()</code>: If id empty → id = L- + String(learnerCounter).padStart(4,'0') → While exists in same school (check learners loop) → learnerCounter++ → id = next → Then push learner, if numPart >= learnerCounter or empty input → learnerCounter++ → save() → Next preview update in renderAll()<br>
<b>At Least 1 Teaching Subject Required:</b> In <code>addStaff()</code>: subjectsRaw = staffSubject input uppercase → Split by comma → Map trim uppercase → Filter length>0 → subjectsArray - If length===0 → alert BLOCKED - At least 1 subject required - Validate each against capsSubjects array but allow invalid with confirm - Store as subject: subjectsArray[0] for backward compat + subjects: subjectsArray array + subjectsRaw original - In <code>issueBook()</code>: Get educator from staff by curUserEmail - educatorSubjects = educator.subjects || [educator.subject] - If length>0: Find bookSubject from books array by code - Check hasSubject loop - If not has → alert BLOCKED - Subject restriction - Return - Else allow issue - Retrieve any allowed in returnBook() - No subject check in return<br>
<b>Simple Numbering ACC-G10-001:</b> bookCounter from localStorage mk_bookCounter - In addBookWithDBECode(): If manual code provided → Use manual - Else for qty loop: num = String(bookCounter).padStart(3,'0') → unique = subject + '-' + grade + '-' + num → books.push with code unique - bookCounter++ - Preview: subject + '-' + grade + '-' + String(bookCounter).padStart(3,'0')<br>
<b>Block EMIS Dup, Allow Name Dup:</b> In addSchool() and uploadDBECSV(): Loop schools array check if schools[i].emis===e → If exists → alert BLOCKED - EMIS DUPLICATE - Return - Else allow - Name dup allowed: No check for name duplicate, only EMIS - Same for learners: Block Learner ID dup per school: Loop learners check if learners[i].id.toUpperCase()===id && learners[i].school===curSchool → If exists → BLOCKED - Else allow - Name dup allowed: No block for same name, only ID per school - Track nameDupCount for info but allow<br>
<b>Permissions:</b> checkPermission(action): If curRank==='ADMIN' return true - If action add_book/remove_book/manage_staff: If curRank==='PRINCIPAL' return true else alert DENIED - If action add_school/add_principal/subscription: If not ADMIN → alert DENIED - If action approve_hod/print_log: If LIBRARIAN/PRINCIPAL/ADMIN/EDUCATOR/HOD return true - If jobs: If PRINCIPAL/ADMIN return true - applyPermissions() disables buttons based on rank<br>
<b>Subscription:</b> subscriptions array {emis, schoolName, town, province, package DEMO/BASIC/PREMIUM/ENTERPRISE, duration 1/3/6/12, amount, status ACTIVE/EXPIRED/PENDING, paidBy, startDate, endDate, startDateObj ISO, endDateObj ISO, addedBy, date} - addSubscription() checks existingIdx for same EMIS → If exists → renewal (replace) else push - Update schools[i].pkg and subscriptionStatus - Revenue sum<br>
<b>Jobs:</b> jobs array {id JOB-xxxxxx, title, description, priority LOW/MEDIUM/HIGH/URGENT, dueDate, assignedEmail, assignedName, assignedRank, assignedSubjects array, assignedSubjectsRaw string, school, schoolName, status PENDING/IN_PROGRESS/COMPLETED, createdBy, date, updatedBy} - addJob() checks curRank PRINCIPAL/ADMIN, checks assignedStaff exists, checks subjects length>0, checks Principal can only assign to own school staff, generates id, pushes, save - updateJobStatus() allows PRINCIPAL/ADMIN/LIBRARIAN or assigned staff to update - Render filters<br>
<b>Printable Records:</b> printIssueRecords() filters by curSchool if not ADMIN, by status BORROWED or TODAY, builds HTML table with learnerName from learners array, bookTitle from books array, signatures table - window.print() - Same for printReturnRecords() filters RETURNED - printCombinedTransactionLog() both - printHodLog() single request - printAllHodLogs() all - printAdminSystemReport() schools performance + staff - printSubscriptionReport() + printJobsReport()
</div>

